    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on speed and favorable platoon matchups, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Yordan Alvarez** (78.29) anchoring the lineup as our most explosive assets. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to a favorable platoon split against a right-handed arm and a projected lead-off spot bolstered by helpful winds, making him the highest-ceiling play on the board. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** leverages his elite 0.476 xwOBA to overcome a slight park disadvantage, providing the necessary thump to support the stolen base upside provided by **Christian Yelich** (75.76), who remains a locked-in starter thanks to his 92% SB efficiency probability against a right-handed starter.\n\nThe decision to start **Caleb Durbin** (63.60) was solidified by the tactical advantage of targeting a slower opposing delivery, which keeps our stolen base potential high in a 5x5 format where every swipe is at a premium. Conversely, the benching of **Nelson Velazquez** (50.22) was the most difficult call of the morning; while his xwOBA of 0.394 is undeniably attractive, he fell just short of our rotation requirements. The optimizer favored the defensive versatility and platoon advantages of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Casey Schmitt** to keep our lineup efficiency above the 50-point threshold. We remain cautious regarding **Junior Caminero** (55.20), whose score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against an elite arm (2.96 xERA), forcing us to temper expectations for his production today. Aside from the volatility inherent in waiting for final lineups for **Dillon Dingler** and **Lars Nootbaar**, the roster is positioned to maximize category gains while protecting our total game caps.",
